<newsitem itemid="121805" id="root" date="1996-10-16" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Burn Stewart profit slumps in year, div cut.</title>
<headline>Burn Stewart profit slumps in year, div cut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		0.94		   vs 4.65</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.7		    vs 3.3</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 3.4		    vs 5.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     1.01		   vs 3.96</p>
<p> Turnover		   54.37		  vs 50.38</p>
<p> Operating profit	 3.93		   vs 6.28</p>
<p> Interest payable	 2.91		   vs 2.33</p>
<p> Tax			  0.46		   vs 1.20</p>
<p> Net taxed		  0.56		   vs 2.76</p>
<p> Retained loss	    1.46		   vs 0.21 loss</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 29</p>
<p> Div registration date  November 5</p>
<p>NOTE - Burn Stewart Distillers Plc said pretax profit figures have been adversely affected by the switch to the FRS 5 accounting standard. The company said that, despite its high gearing, its bankers, Bank of Scotland, have indicated continued strong support. Burn Stewart said that when profits excluded from this year's results is included , it will &quot;consider the most appropriate means of reflecting this profit in our ongoing dividend policy.&quot; -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
</text>
